WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:07.180
Speaker 1: David, I've noticed that the term
gaslighting now seems to be used too much.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.190
Has it become problematic or even meaningless?

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.960
Yeah, this is this is a good question.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.270
What's going on with the term gaslighting
is similar to what went on with Regressive

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.320
left a few years ago.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.630
And I'll explain what I mean by that.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:25.510
Gaslighting is when you manipulate someone
to get them to question their own sanity or

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:28.150
whether they can even trust just the most
basic facts.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.170
They thought they believed it.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:34.460
Sort of like, you know, you have very mundane
level.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:41.060
You ask your significant other never to wear
shoes in the house 50 times, and then they

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.330
wear shoes in the house.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:49.410
And then they you say, you know, I we've talked
about this so many times and they say we haven't

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.410
talked about it.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.550
When one was that I don't remember.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.550
Right.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.550
Just like we did we did.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.800
I imagine the 50 conversations, just a mundane
example.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:03.730
But it can happen with a whole bunch of other
issues, political, social, cultural, et cetera,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.530
that we are seeing something happen with the
term gaslighting that similar to regressive

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.770
left, there was a very, very short period.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.330
And we talked about this in a long form piece
about the progressive left where the term

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:22.090
regressive left really meant someone who is
ostensibly on the left, but who is failing

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.090
to really do it.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:30.700
For example, sometimes a self-described leftist
will support very authoritarian policy or

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.409
authoritarian elected officials or world leaders.

00:01:34.409 --> 00:01:38.820
And we would say this is this is regressive
left in the sense that they claim to be left,

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.170
but they're really just authoritarian.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:44.540
OK, yeah, it had some kind of meaning there.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:51.010
It became a catchall for people who we disagree
with, and it was used by the right and by

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.770
the left, and it became essentially meaningless.

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:54.770
I stopped using it.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:59.610
I used it very, very briefly to describe a
very specific thing.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:05.140
Racism is another one where there's this trend
that we're starting to see, where someone

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.780
will identify something they believe is racist.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.230
They will be called racist for noticing it.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.480
Sometimes you will hear this from the right.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.140
Well, they will say you noticing race so much.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:24.700
Is a sign that you are the racist and a very
similar dynamic is happening now with gaslighting,

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:29.840
if you say something is gaslighting, you will
sometimes be called the gas lighter.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.110
You will say your gaslighting people.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:39.200
By claiming that gaslighting is taking place,
you are manipulating you were virtue signaling

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.560
by using that term.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:45.940
And a very, very similar kind of vicious circle
starts.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:48.900
And it does devalue the term in a significant
way.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:55.790
So I think there is still value, you know,
regressive left is now in the trash as a term.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:01.989
I still think that gaslighting has value and
there is still real objective empirical meaning

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:06.990
that is useful to us in describing, you know,
there was a lot of gaslighting by the Trumpy

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.150
and right.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.459
About just telling people what your Trump
said, what you are seeing and hearing.

00:03:11.459 --> 00:03:15.670
You cannot believe that's a form of gaslighting.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.770
And I think it still has value.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:22.170
But they're making every effort to devalue
it, calling it calling the use of the term

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.220
an actual gaslight in and of itself.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.410
And all of these terms have a shelf life.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.320
That's the that's the reality.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.620
So let me know your experiences with the term,
either using it or having it used on you or

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.060
having it used merely to muddle up conversations.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.209
We have a great bonus show for you today.

